# Line-ending policy for tracked data files.
#
# CSVs are hashed for provenance: data/raw/SHA256SUMS.txt records their digests,
# and preprocess_data() stores an input digest under data_provenance. Without a
# policy here, git's autocrlf smudge gives a checkout CRLF on Windows and LF
# elsewhere, so the same tracked file has different bytes -- and a different
# SHA-256 -- depending on who cloned it. Recorded digests then verify on one
# platform only.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to LF everywhere and normalizes on commit, so an
# editor that writes CRLF cannot reintroduce the drift. This also makes the CSV
# bundled in the wheel (prism/data/) byte-identical regardless of build host.
#
# Verified safe when this was applied: every newline in every tracked CSV was a
# row terminator (no CR inside a quoted field), so normalizing changes framing
# only, not values. Re-check that before adding a CSV with multi-line fields.
*.csv text eol=lf
